<title>IRAQ: IRAQ SAYS TO EXPORT 30 MLN BLS OIL BY END AUGUST.</title>
<headline>IRAQ SAYS TO EXPORT 30 MLN BLS OIL BY END AUGUST.</headline>
<dateline>BAGHDAD 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq said on Monday 18 tankers were expected to load 30 million barrels of crude oil for export under the United Nations oil-for-food deal by the end of August.</p>
<p>Oil minister Amir Muhammed Rasheed said the first two-million barrel shipment from the Turkish port of Ceyhan was expected in the next two days once the contract has been approved by the U.N. sanctions committee.</p>
</text>
